'''box'''<sup>3</sup> (boks), ''v.'' [< ''box''<sup>3</sup>, ''n.'' Cf. F. ''boxer'' = D. ''boksen'' = LG. ''baaksen'' = Icel. ''byxa'' = Norw. ''baksa'' = Sw. ''baxa'' = Dan. ''baxe'' = G. ''baxen'', ''boxen'', all < E. ''box''<sup>3</sup>.] '''I.''' ''trans.'' To beat; thrash; strike with the fist or hand; especially, to strike on the ear or side of the head: as, “they ''box'' her about the ears,” ''North'', tr. of Plutarch, p. 115.
{{smaller block|By heaven! a little thing would make me ''box'' you.
{{right|''Chapman'', Gentleman Usher, iii. 1.}}}}

